.SS "template<uint32_t dim> bool csmp::SKUA_FiniteElementMeshInterface::ReadPropertyRecordsASCII (ifstream & ifs, \fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"
Method reads a single property record into a \fBPropertyData\fP object and adds the data to the argument \fBVSet\fP\&.

.PP
Each property record consists of :

.PP
name(string) placement(enum PLACEMENT) type (\fBVARIABLE_TYPE\fP) (array length (int32)) number of data entries (int32) flag values (int32) property values (double)

.PP
for variable placement and type, upper case or lower case spellings are accepted\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
While space in variable names is expressed by an underscore which gets removed in CSMP\&.

.PP
At this point, no range check is performed on the values read, but parsing errors related to variable placement, type and flags are reported\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
A reference to the initialized ASCII input file stream\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true when the record was read correctly and completely\&.
.RE
.PP
